# Copy to .release-request (gitignored) and edit, then: open tools/release.command
#
# COMPONENTS is cut in order. Each one's marker commit is pushed before the next
# starts — release.sh never pushes, and its cut-origin guard refuses to cut while
# this repo is ahead of its remote, so an unpushed marker strands the rest.
#
# A component whose source has not changed since its last cut resolves to the
# same stamp, whose tag already exists, and is refused. That is a no-op, not a
# failure to work around: drop it from COMPONENTS, or pass --force in FLAGS if
# you genuinely mean to re-cut it.

COMPONENTS="edge"
FLAGS="--public"
